Reduced the work an IP Fabric sync does per object further. An unchanged IP Address, Interface, VLAN, Location or Cable is stamped with one update rather than a validated save worth about eleven queries, a new Cable is written once rather than twice, resolving an address reads the address table once rather than twice, and the Status and LocationType checks a VLAN needs are resolved once for the run rather than once per VLAN. Objects queued for deletion are held as a model and primary key rather than as loaded instances, which on a large teardown were retained with everything their queryset selected alongside them.
